IMPORT prelude

-- Child Care Services Act 2007 (Western Australia) -- which child care the Act still governs now that the Education and
-- Care Services National Law (WA) governs long day care, family day care and outside school hours care (ss 3, 4, 5B);
-- whether the service must be licensed (ss 9, 13, 21, 22(3), 45(1)(a)); and what the parent can rely on from a licensed
-- service (s 18 supervision, s 36 advertising, s 29(4)(b)(ii) refunds, s 25(3) suspensions, s 45A(3) publication).
--
-- SEAT: the parent using child care -- the person who "at law has responsibility for" the child's care (s 3 "parent"),
-- asking about the service their child attends. Every decision is phrased as that parent would ask it: "Which law
-- governs the service my child attends", "Must it be licensed", "Is it lawfully provided", "Could I get my fees back".
-- The Act addresses providers and the CEO; what it means for the parent is encoded.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 (child care service, licence, parent, national child care law), s 4, s 5B(1), (2), s 9 and
-- its penalty, s 13(1), s 18, s 21(1), s 22(3), s 25(3)(b), (4), s 28, s 29(2), (4)(b)(ii), (5), s 36, s 45(1)(a), (3B),
-- s 45A(3).
--
-- Edition: the compilation as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49333.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026),
-- which includes the Education and Care Services National Law Application Act 2026 (No. 2 of 2026, in force 1 May
-- 2026). The National Law's definitions of "education and care service", "personal arrangement" and "associated
-- children's service", and its s 103, are read from the deposited Education and Care Services National Law (WA),
-- ../../../education-and-care-services-national-law-wa/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49389.txt (retrieved 7 September
-- 2026). The Child Care Services regulations (which prescribe the types of service the Act applies to, s 4(b), and any
-- other age limit) are NOT deposited, so whether a service is prescribed is an input.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the licence application and grant tests (ss 10-17) except as they matter to the parent; renewal
-- procedure (ss 23A-24); disciplinary action against managerial officers (ss 30C, 30D); review by SAT (s 30, open to
-- the applicant or licensee, not the parent); licence documents (ss 31-35); Part 3 administration; Part 4 compliance
-- and enforcement powers; ss 46-53D (records in proceedings, offences of obstruction, regulations, codes of practice);
-- Part 6 transitional provisions. Everything about a service under the National Law beyond whether it needs a service
-- approval -- quality ratings, staffing ratios, the parent's rights under the National Regulations -- is for the
-- National Law's own encoding. The Child Care Subsidy is the A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999's.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Child Care Services Act 2007 -- the parent's questions`

§§ `Terms -- the service, who gives the care, and the National Law's exclusions`

-- National Law s 5 "personal arrangement": education and care provided "(a) by a family member or guardian of a child
-- personally, otherwise than as a staff member of, or under an engagement with, a service ...; or (b) by a friend of
-- the family of the child personally under an informal arrangement where no offer to provide that education and care
-- was advertised".
DECLARE `Who gives the care` IS ONE OF
    `a family member or guardian, personally`                       -- personal arrangement, limb (a)
    `a family friend, personally, informally, with no advertised offer` -- personal arrangement, limb (b)
    `a family friend who advertised the offer`                      -- not a personal arrangement
    `a business, organisation or public body`                       -- not a personal arrangement

-- National Law s 5 "education and care service": any service providing education and care on a regular basis to
-- children under 13, "other than" (a) a school's educational program; (b) a community kindergarten's; (c) a personal
-- arrangement (asked through `Who gives the care`); (d) "a service principally conducted to provide instruction in a
-- particular activity" (sport, dance, music, culture, language, religion); (e) care of patients in a hospital or of a
-- medical or therapeutic care service; (f) care under a child protection law; (g) a prescribed class of disability
-- service; (h) a service of a prescribed class.
DECLARE `National Law exclusion` IS ONE OF
    `none of the exclusions`
    `a school providing an educational program`
    `a community kindergarten`
    `instruction in a particular activity`
    `care of hospital or therapy patients`
    `care under a child protection law`
    `a prescribed disability service or other prescribed class`

-- One case is one service the child attends.
DECLARE Service HAS
    `it provides education and care on a regular basis`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the children are under 13`                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 4: 13, "or such other age as may be prescribed"
    `who gives the care`                                  IS A `Who gives the care`
    `the exclusion`                                       IS A `National Law exclusion`
    `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(b); regulations not deposited
    `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run` IS A BOOLEAN  -- associated children's service

GIVEN s IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a personal arrangement` IF
    CONSIDER s's `who gives the care`
    WHEN `a family member or guardian, personally` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a family friend, personally, informally, with no advertised offer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN s IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is regular education and care of children under 13` IF
    s's `it provides education and care on a regular basis` AND s's `the children are under 13`

-- National Law s 5: "education and care service". Examples in the Law: "long day care services, family day care
-- services and outside school hours services, unless expressly excluded".
GIVEN s IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an education and care service under the National Law` IF
        `it is regular education and care of children under 13` s
    AND (NOT (`it is a personal arrangement` s))
    AND s's `the exclusion` EQUALS `none of the exclusions`

-- s 4: "a child care service is a service providing or intended to provide education and care on a regular basis to
-- children under 13 years of age ... that -- (a) is not an education and care service under the national child care
-- law; and (b) is prescribed for the purposes of this Act as a type of service to which this Act applies."
@export Is the service my child attends a child care service under the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 4?
GIVEN s IS A Service @desc The service your child attends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a child care service under this Act` IF
        `it is regular education and care of children under 13` s
    AND (NOT (`it is an education and care service under the National Law` s))
    AND s's `the regulations prescribe it as a type this Act applies to`

-- National Law s 5 "associated children's service": "a children's service that is operated or intended to be operated
-- by an approved provider at the same place as an approved education and care service".
GIVEN s IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an associated children's service` IF
        `Is it a child care service under this Act` s
    AND s's `it is run by an approved provider where an approved education and care service is run`

§§ `ss 4, 5B -- which law governs the service my child attends`

-- s 5B(1): "This Act does not apply to a child care service that is an associated children's service to the extent
-- to which the national child care law applies to that service." (2): subject to (1), the Act applies "as if" the
-- service approval "were a licence under this Act", the approved provider "were a holder of a licence", and the
-- nominated supervisor "were a supervising officer".
DECLARE `The law that governs it` IS ONE OF
    `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
    `this Act, as a child care service`
    `this Act, as an associated children's service, so far as the National Law does not apply`
    `neither this Act nor the National Law`

@export Which law governs the child care service my child attends -- the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) or the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)?
GIVEN s IS A Service @desc The service your child attends
GIVETH A `The law that governs it`
DECIDE `Which law governs the service my child attends` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an education and care service under the National Law` s
            THEN `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
        IF `it is an associated children's service` s
            THEN `this Act, as an associated children's service, so far as the National Law does not apply`
        IF `Is it a child care service under this Act` s
            THEN `this Act, as a child care service`
        OTHERWISE `neither this Act nor the National Law`

§§ `ss 9, 45, 5B(2) -- must the service be licensed`

-- s 9: "A person must not provide a child care service at a place except under and in accordance with a licence
-- authorising the provision of the service at that place."
-- s 45(1)(a): the Minister may, by order published in the Gazette, exempt a specified child care service, or a type,
-- from s 9.
-- National Law s 103(1): a person must not provide an education and care service unless an approved provider of an
-- approved education and care service.
DECLARE `What licence it needs` IS ONE OF
    `a licence under s 9 for this service at this place`
    `none: it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order under s 45`
    `its National Law service approval counts as its licence (s 5B(2))`
    `none under this Act: the National Law requires a provider approval and service approval instead (s 103)`
    `none: neither this Act nor the National Law requires one`

@export Must the service my child attends hold a licence under the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA)?
GIVEN s IS A Service @desc The service your child attends
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order published in the Gazette under s 45(1)(a) exempts this service, or its type, from s 9
GIVETH A `What licence it needs`
DECIDE `Must the service hold a licence` IS
    CONSIDER `Which law governs the service my child attends` s
    WHEN `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`
        THEN `none under this Act: the National Law requires a provider approval and service approval instead (s 103)`
    WHEN `this Act, as an associated children's service, so far as the National Law does not apply`
        THEN `its National Law service approval counts as its licence (s 5B(2))`
    WHEN `this Act, as a child care service`
        THEN IF `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`
                THEN `none: it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order under s 45`
                ELSE `a licence under s 9 for this service at this place`
    WHEN `neither this Act nor the National Law`
        THEN `none: neither this Act nor the National Law requires one`

§§ `ss 13, 21, 22(3), 28, 45(3B) -- is the service lawfully provided under this Act`

-- s 13(1): a licence authorises "a specified type of child care service at a specified place".
-- s 21(1): a licence has effect for the period in the licence document unless suspended, cancelled or surrendered;
-- s 22(3): if a renewal application is made in accordance with s 22(2), "the licence continues to have effect until the
-- renewal application is determined" unless suspended or cancelled. s 28: a suspension lasts until revoked, or the
-- licence is cancelled, expires or is surrendered.
-- For an associated children's service, "the licence" is its National Law service approval (s 5B(2)(a)).
DECLARE `Licence status` IS ONE OF
    `in effect`
    `its period has ended, but a renewal was lodged in time and is undecided`  -- still in effect, s 22(3)
    `its period has ended and no renewal was lodged in time`
    `suspended`
    `cancelled`
    `surrendered`
    `no licence held`

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Licence status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence has effect` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `in effect` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `its period has ended, but a renewal was lodged in time and is undecided` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Is it lawful` IS ONE OF
    `yes: under a licence that has effect`
    `yes: under a Ministerial exemption`
    `no: provided without a licence that has effect for it here (s 9 offence)`
    `no: provided in breach of the licence (s 9; s 20 offence)`
    `no: provided in breach of the exemption's conditions (s 45(3B) offence)`
    `not for this Act: the National Law governs it`
    `not for this Act: neither this Act nor the National Law governs it`

@export Is the service my child attends being provided lawfully under the Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA)?
GIVEN s IS A Service @desc The service your child attends
      `the status` IS A `Licence status` @desc The state of the service's licence (for an associated children's service, its National Law service approval)
      `the licence is for this type of service at this place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence names this type of service and this place (s 13(1))
      `it is run in accordance with the licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is being run in accordance with its licence and its conditions
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order under s 45(1)(a) exempts the service from s 9
      `it complies with the exemption's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service complies with any conditions in that order (s 45(3B))
GIVETH A `Is it lawful`
DECIDE `Is the service lawfully provided under this Act` IS
    CONSIDER `Which law governs the service my child attends` s
    WHEN `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)` THEN `not for this Act: the National Law governs it`
    WHEN `neither this Act nor the National Law` THEN `not for this Act: neither this Act nor the National Law governs it`
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `the licence is for this type of service at this place` AND `the licence has effect` `the status`
                THEN IF `it is run in accordance with the licence`
                        THEN `yes: under a licence that has effect`
                        ELSE `no: provided in breach of the licence (s 9; s 20 offence)`
            IF `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`
                THEN IF `it complies with the exemption's conditions`
                        THEN `yes: under a Ministerial exemption`
                        ELSE `no: provided in breach of the exemption's conditions (s 45(3B) offence)`
            OTHERWISE `no: provided without a licence that has effect for it here (s 9 offence)`

§§ `s 9 penalty -- what the provider faces for running an unlicensed service`

-- s 9 Penalty: "(a) for a first offence -- (i) a fine of $12 000 and imprisonment for one year; and (ii) a daily penalty
-- of $600; (b) for a subsequent offence -- (i) a fine of $24 000 and imprisonment for 2 years; and (ii) a daily penalty
-- of $1 200."
DECLARE `Penalty` HAS
    `fine in dollars`          IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment in months`   IS A NUMBER
    `daily penalty in dollars` IS A NUMBER

@export What is the most the provider of my child's service can be fined for providing it without a licence (s 9), in dollars?
GIVEN `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be the provider's first s 9 offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the provider can be fined for running unlicensed` IS
    (`the s 9 penalty` `it is a first offence`)'s `fine in dollars`

@export What is the daily penalty the provider of my child's service faces for each day it runs without a licence (s 9), in dollars?
GIVEN `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be the provider's first s 9 offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the daily penalty for running unlicensed` IS
    (`the s 9 penalty` `it is a first offence`)'s `daily penalty in dollars`

@export What is the longest the provider of my child's service can be imprisoned for providing it without a licence (s 9), in months?
GIVEN `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be the provider's first s 9 offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest the provider can be imprisoned for running unlicensed` IS
    (`the s 9 penalty` `it is a first offence`)'s `imprisonment in months`

GIVEN `it is a first offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty`
DECIDE `the s 9 penalty` IS
    IF `it is a first offence`
        THEN `Penalty` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 12000, `imprisonment in months` IS 12, `daily penalty in dollars` IS 600
        ELSE `Penalty` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 24000, `imprisonment in months` IS 24, `daily penalty in dollars` IS 1200

§§ `s 18 -- the supervising officer must be there`

-- s 18: "It is a condition of every licence that the licensee must ensure that the supervising officer for the child
-- care service is present at the place where the service is provided at the times when the service is provided except
-- to the extent (if any) that the regulations otherwise provide." For an associated children's service, the nominated
-- supervisor is read as the supervising officer (s 5B(2)(d)).
@export Must the supervising officer be present while the service is caring for my child (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 18)?
GIVEN s IS A Service @desc The service your child attends
      `the regulations provide otherwise for this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations relieve the licensee of the s 18 condition at this time (regulations not deposited)
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order under s 45(1)(a) exempts the service from s 9 (an exempt service holds no licence, so has no licence condition)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the supervising officer be present` IF
        (NOT (`Which law governs the service my child attends` s EQUALS `the Education and Care Services National Law (WA)`))
    AND (NOT (`Which law governs the service my child attends` s EQUALS `neither this Act nor the National Law`))
    AND (NOT `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`)
    AND (NOT `the regulations provide otherwise for this time`)

§§ `s 36 -- may it advertise itself as a child care service`

-- s 36: "A person must not advertise, or otherwise hold out in any way, that the person provides a child care service
-- unless -- (a) the person holds a licence authorising the provision of the child care service; or (b) the person is
-- not required to hold a licence ... because of an exemption under section 45(1)(a)." Penalty: a fine of $6 000.
@export May the provider advertise that it provides the child care service (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 36)?
GIVEN `it holds a licence authorising the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider holds a licence authorising the service it advertises
      `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order under s 45(1)(a) exempts the service from s 9
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the provider advertise the service` IF
    `it holds a licence authorising the service` OR `it is exempted from s 9 by a Ministerial order`

§§ `s 29 -- could I get my fees back`

-- s 29(2): grounds for disciplinary action against a licensee exist if (a) the licensee "improperly obtained a licence";
-- (b) "contravened this Act"; (c) the CEO is no longer satisfied as to a matter in s 14(3), 15(2) or 16(2); (d)
-- contravened the Working with Children (Screening) Act 2004 s 22; or (e) "there are reasonable grounds for believing
-- that the continued provision of the child care service ... would constitute an unacceptable risk to the wellbeing of
-- the children". (4)(b)(ii): the State Administrative Tribunal, "if satisfied that grounds for disciplinary action
-- exist", may order the person to "refund to a specified person or body fees or other money received from that person
-- or body in connection with the provision of the child care service". (5): that order may be made "whether or not at
-- the time when the order is made the person is a licensee". The CEO decides whether to allege (s 29(3)); the parent
-- cannot. Both judgments are answered conditionally.
DECLARE `Fee refund` IS ONE OF
    `possible: the Tribunal may order the licensee to refund my fees, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist`
    `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated`
    `not under this Act: it does not license the service`

@export Could the provider of my child's service be ordered to refund my fees (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 29(4)(b)(ii))?
GIVEN s IS A Service @desc The service your child attends
      `the licensee improperly obtained the licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee improperly obtained its licence (s 29(2)(a))
      `the licensee contravened this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee contravened the Child Care Services Act 2007 (s 29(2)(b))
      `the CEO is no longer satisfied of a licensing matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO is no longer satisfied as to a matter in s 14(3), 15(2) or 16(2) that was relevant to granting the licence (s 29(2)(c))
      `the licensee contravened the Working with Children Act s 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee contravened the Working with Children (Screening) Act 2004 s 22 (s 29(2)(d))
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe continued care is an unacceptable risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are reasonable grounds for believing that continuing the service would be an unacceptable risk to the children's wellbeing (s 29(2)(e))
GIVETH A `Fee refund`
DECIDE `Could I be refunded my fees` IS
    IF (NOT (`Must the service hold a licence` s FALSE EQUALS `a licence under s 9 for this service at this place`))
       AND (NOT (`Must the service hold a licence` s FALSE EQUALS `its National Law service approval counts as its licence (s 5B(2))`))
        THEN `not under this Act: it does not license the service`
        ELSE IF    `the licensee improperly obtained the licence`
                OR `the licensee contravened this Act`
                OR `the CEO is no longer satisfied of a licensing matter`
                OR `the licensee contravened the Working with Children Act s 22`
                OR `there are reasonable grounds to believe continued care is an unacceptable risk`
                THEN `possible: the Tribunal may order the licensee to refund my fees, if the CEO alleges and the Tribunal is satisfied grounds exist`
                ELSE `no: no ground for disciplinary action is stated`

§§ `ss 25, 45A -- suspension, and what may be published`

-- s 25(1): the CEO may suspend a licence on reasonable grounds of unacceptable risk, with or without hearing the licensee
-- (s 25(2)); (3)(b) the notice "must specify the period of the suspension, which must not exceed 60 days"; (4) within 21
-- days the CEO must, unless the suspension is revoked, make an allegation to the State Administrative Tribunal, which may
-- confirm, revoke or extend it (s 25(6)).
@export For how many days at most can the CEO suspend my child's service's licence by notice (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 25(3)(b))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest the CEO can suspend the licence in days` IS 60

@export Within how many days of suspending the licence must the CEO take the matter to the State Administrative Tribunal, unless the suspension is revoked (s 25(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must the CEO go to the Tribunal` IS 21

-- s 45A(3): "Information published under this section may identify a particular child care service or a particular
-- person, but not a child."
@export May the CEO publish information about child care services that identifies my child (Child Care Services Act 2007 (WA) s 45A(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the CEO publish information identifying my child` IF FALSE
